From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:16:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: ucode: report interface enable failures

Return the result of the synchronous enable operation to the ucode
caller, which may need to fall back from a station-provided channel.
An accepted enable can still complete asynchronously after ACS or CAC.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/ap/ucode.c
+++ b/src/ap/ucode.c
@@ -851,10 +851,8 @@
 	if (conf->channel && !iface->freq)
 		iface->freq = hostapd_hw_get_freq(iface->bss[0], conf->channel);
 
-	if (iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED) {
-		hostapd_enable_iface(iface);
-		return ucv_boolean_new(true);
-	}
+	if (iface->state != HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED)
+		return ucv_boolean_new(hostapd_enable_iface(iface) >= 0);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < iface->num_bss; i++) {
 		struct hostapd_data *hapd = iface->bss[i];
